  "answer_markdown": "To investigate who deleted conversations programmatically, the administrator should query the audit logs for the event type `le_chat.conversation.deleted`. This event type records when a le Chat conversation is deleted [4].\n\nTo narrow results to a specific human user, they can use the `actor_user_uuid` query parameter, which filters logs by the UUID of the user who performed the action [2,6].\n\nBy default, each request returns 20 entries [2,6].\n\n### Example API Request\n```\nGET /audit-logs\n?event_type=le_chat.conversation.deleted\n&actor_user_uuid=<user_uuid>\n&limit=20\n```\n\nWhere `<user_uuid>` is the unique identifier of the human user being investigated.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Filter logs by the UUID of the user who performed the action"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "Records when a le Chat conversation is deleted"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "quote": "Filter logs by the UUID of the user who performed the action"
    }
  ],
